:{"text":"This is going to be a guide to lighting upgrades for an 1987 Dodge Raider/Mitsubishi Montero 2.6L with a Weber carburetor and standard options. Otherwise known as a generation 1 Montero, Pajero, or Raider.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5n1r6","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4gjgf","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"On todays post we are going to talk about lighting in better detail. Why we upgrade is important. My personal decision to spend money on this project stems from the idea of knowing where to go in the dark. LED is a great way to do this as they use less power then conventional and are much brighter. They also have a much longer life compared to traditional bulbs. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3l86b","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"difhu","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"They can be used in many ways, while on the trails, when lighting the camp ground, or working on another car etc. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ibs9","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"48bad","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Bulb color is a personal choice to note as well. I went with white output however some folks prefer yellow output foe fog lights and so on. Certain colors can help with different driving condition. In the end they have bulbs of many colors for folks to express them self's or for what they want them for.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"1bptj","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8jjom","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"When it comes to wiring please use proper gauge wiring for the load you put on it (Amperage/Wattage). For instance the wiring to the fuse box needs 10 gauge wiring while the rest of system I can use 16 or 14 gauge without pushing the limits of the wiring. I will attach some images below.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5007p","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c3gjc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Please continue down below for more info. If you like what you see please like and subscribe has it lets me know people find this helpful.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dotj","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8ge78","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Thanks, ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"abio4","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Edna","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"61om3","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"1isf7","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"*Please note these are not/maybe the exact products used but are the same compatibility. Please pick out and confirm that the items you like will work with your install. As you may have a different setup or additional options.*","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5apau","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7a0v1","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Part 1-General Updates for Future Additions","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"UNDERLINE","underlineData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"70d81","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"The video below shows my setups test layout in the Raider. It is a completely functional setup other then I had to fiddle with the fuel pump relay that it would only turn on at a certain voltage instead of the keyed on state via relay.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"VIDEO","id":"4gmif","nodes":[],"videoData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"video":{"src":{"id":"video/42cca7_7acc6babf5234b75872c8dab4fa2e527/720p/mp4/file.mp4"},"duration":64.273},"thumbnail":{"src":{"id":"media/42cca7_7acc6babf5234b75872c8dab4fa2e527f000.jpg"},"width":1600,"height":900}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ak07u","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"The image below is my listed specifications of my amperage draw and the ability's of the wiring in the system. Please note when you go ordering lighting for your rig it may list a crazy number like \"2000 watt lighting!\" however the folks that make lighting can mean that it is 2000 watts equivalent and due to it being LED it will use much less power. In this way you should always measure your amperage using a volt meter to get a accurate rating of the proper wattage draw of your lighting. FYI KO=Keyed Off and this image isn't fully updated after a few changes to the system.","decorations":[]}}],"paragra